awk: line 1: syntax error at or near ,
awk: line 1: syntax error at or near }

Think: Collect hardware metadata (uname, /proc/cpuinfo, /proc/meminfo) and write a JSON file temp_sys_info/sys_meta.json in one awk command, also counting CPUs.

Act: bash

```bash
awk -v uname="$(uname -a)" 'BEGIN{
  cpuinfo=""; meminfo=""; cpu_count=0;
  while((getline line < "/proc/cpuinfo")>0){
    gsub(/\\/,"\\\\",line); gsub(/"/,"\\\"",line);
    cpuinfo = cpuinfo line "\\n";
    if(line ~ /^processor[[:space:]]*:/) cpu_count++;
  }
  close("/proc/cpuinfo");
  while((getline line < "/proc/meminfo")>0){
    gsub(/\\/,"\\\\",line); gsub(/"/,"\\\"",line);
    meminfo = meminfo line "\\n";
  }
  close("/proc/meminfo");
  print "{"; 
  print "\"uname\": \"" uname "\","; 
  print "\"cpu_count\": " cpu_count ",";
  print "\"cpuinfo\": \"" cpuinfo "\","; 
  print "\"meminfo\": \"" meminfo "\"";
  print "}";
}' > temp_sys_info/sys_meta.json
```

